<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>West Virginia Claims Third Straight NCAA Mid-Atlantic Regional Title</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/13/cross-country-west-virginia-claims-third-straight-ncaa-mid-atlantic-regional-title</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/13/cross-country-west-virginia-claims-third-straight-ncaa-mid-atlantic-regional-title</guid><category>Cross Country</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The cross country team poses after winning the NCAA Mid-Atlantic Regional championship." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/13/MSoc_WVUvsCoastalCarolina_Nov11_2026_TT-10.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 3 West Virginia University cross country team claimed its third consecutive NCAA Mid-Atlantic Regional championship on Friday, Nov. 13, at the Goodman Campus Cross Country Course in Bethlehem, Pa.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/13/MSoc_WVUvsCoastalCarolina_Nov11_2026_TT-10.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/13/MSoc_WVUvsCoastalCarolina_Nov11_2026_TT-10.jpg"><media:title>The cross country team poses after winning the NCAA Mid-Atlantic Regional championship.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/13/MSoc_WVUvsCoastalCarolina_Nov11_2026_TT-10.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:44:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>10</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59692</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Welcome Nation's Top Teams for Fall Classic</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/13/rifle-mountaineers-welcome-nations-top-teams-for-fall-classic</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/13/rifle-mountaineers-welcome-nations-top-teams-for-fall-classic</guid><category>Rifle</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Hana Strakusek competes in smallbore during the mountaineers home opener" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DSC07684.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 1-ranked West Virginia University rifle team is set for its annual WVU Fall Classic on Saturday and Sunday to close out the fall slate of competition. This year, the Mountaineers play host to some of the nation's top teams in No. 2 Ole Miss, No. 6 Kentucky, No. 8 TCU and No. 12 Nebraska at the Bill McKenzie Rifle Range inside the WVU Shell Building in Morgantown.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DSC07684.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DSC07684.jpg"><media:title>Hana Strakusek competes in smallbore during the mountaineers home opener</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DSC07684.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>8</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59683</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Earn Second Straight Victory in Road Test at Houston</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/12/volleyball-mountaineers-earn-second-straight-victory-in-road-test-at-houston</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/12/volleyball-mountaineers-earn-second-straight-victory-in-road-test-at-houston</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Cami Huff celebrates after a point in the win over Houston" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DAK06157.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-10, 6-7 Big 12) earned a 3-1 victory over Houston on Thursday night at the Fertitta Center in Houston, Texas, winning by set scores of 25-21, 22-25, 25-18 and 25-22.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DAK06157.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DAK06157.jpg"><media:title>Cami Huff celebrates after a point in the win over Houston</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/DAK06157.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:58:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59689</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Improve to 3-0 With Thursday Night’s Victory Over Mercer</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/12/mens-basketball-mountaineers-improve-to-3-0-with-thursday-nights-victory-over-mercer</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/12/mens-basketball-mountaineers-improve-to-3-0-with-thursday-nights-victory-over-mercer</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Finley Bizjack scores two of his team-best 15 points in West Virginia's victory over Mercer at Hope Coliseum on Thursday, Nov. 12, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/12/Bizjack-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia used 15 points from Finley Bizjack to down pesky Mercer 75-61 Thursday night at Hope Coliseum.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/Bizjack-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/Bizjack-Main.jpg"><media:title>Finley Bizjack scores two of his team-best 15 points in West Virginia's victory over Mercer at Hope Coliseum on Thursday, Nov. 12, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/Bizjack-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:42:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59688</s:story_id></item><item><title>Greeny Adds Four in National Signing Period</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/12/volleyball-greeny-adds-four-in-national-signing-period</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/12/volleyball-greeny-adds-four-in-national-signing-period</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Jen Greeny adds four players in 2027 Volleyball Signing Class" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/12/VB26_SigningDay_1920x1080.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia University volleyball coach Jen Greeny has announced the addition of four students-athletes for the 2027 season.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/12/VB26_SigningDay_1920x1080.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/202